            "review_title": "Review at Com Hien Nhi Restaurant",
            "review_text": "V H\nSeattle, Washington120 contributions\n0\nExcellence value - Viethanese home cokking\nApr 2015 • Family\nA busy local Vietnamese home cooking restaurant at the corner of Yersin and Hoang Hoa Tham. This is popular with the local. Don't expect a wide variety of dishes like Pho Noodle soup or grilled BBQ. Their menu is \"in the house\". Vietnamese home cooking consisted of some protein dishes (you get fresh fish, shrimp, chicken, pork dishes etc..), vegetable dishes (morning glory, sweet potato shoot, peashoot, egg plant etc..), soup (sour soup, bitter melon, cabbage) and the usual plate of fresh salad/herb.\nMy dad and I (we are Vietnamese) came here for early dinner - Open at 5pm, we ordered two beer, sour fish soup, pork/egg stew, caramelized anchovy and stirred fried sweetpotato shoot, with rice. The food was delicious and the bill came to $10.\nFor those that are budget conscious, you can get a plate of rice with 1 item and a soup for $2.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 27, 2015",
